\n\n## Description\n...Investigation that resolves whether the existing engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) implements the approach described in the strategy, and how much of it can be reused in the formal implementation. The outcome determines the implementation basis (adapt prototype code vs. build from scratch following established dashboard patterns) for the Feature Store admin UI pages.\n\n## Scope\n- Review the prototype PR against the strategy's technical approach: K8s API pass-through CRUD via /api/k8s/*, read proxy /api/featurestores, RBAC model, feature flag gating, page structure (list, wizard, detail, delete)\n- Identify reusable components, divergences, and gaps\n- Produce a reuse assessment / migration recommendation consumed by the frontend implementation work\n- Confirm with Dashboard and Feature Store engineering leads\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- A written assessment exists that maps each prototype capability to the strategy approach (aligned / divergent / absent)\n- A reuse recommendation with a defensible rationale is delivered and confirmed by engineering leads\n- The assessment identifies any architectural divergence that would change the formal implementation approach\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- Supporting: P0 HLRs (create wizard, list, inspect, delete, deployment progress) — the outcome determines how, not whether, they are built\n\nInvestigation signals rationale file.\n\nE002 body:\n\n# Decide TP Form Field Scope and Supported Backend Combinations\n\n## Description\nInvestigation that decides which FeatureStore CRD (feast.dev/v1) fields the TP create wizard exposes (full spec vs curated subset) and which backend combinations (registry type, online/offline store backends, authorization mode) are supported or restricted for production readiness. Deliverable: field-set and validation-constraint spec that the wizard design and implementation build against.\n\n## Scope\n- Enumerate FeatureStore CRD spec fields (registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, TLS, scaling, materialization schedule) from the CRD OpenAPI schema\n- Decide the TP-exposed field set (product decision: full vs curated subset)\n- Identify backend combinations to restrict or warn about (e.g., SQLite as development-only)\n- Deliver a field-set and constraint spec for the create wizard\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- A field-set spec exists listing every FeatureStore CRD field exposed in the TP wizard, with rationale\n- Restricted/unsupported backend combinations are enumerated with guidance\n- The decision is confirmed by PM and Feature Store Engineering\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- P0: guided form wizard field coverage (determines scope)\n- P2: inline validation guidance (constraint source)\n\nE003:\n\n# UXD Wireframes and Interaction Design for Feature Store Admin UI\n\n## Description\nDesign deliverables for the Feature Store admin UI: wireframes and interaction patterns for the create wizard, management list page, detail/inspect view, and delete confirmation dialog, covering admin and viewer (read-only) states. Uses the existing prototype as a starting design reference. Blocked by form field-scope decision (wizard design reflects the decided field set).\n\n## Scope\n- Wireframes: create form wizard (reflecting decided TP field set), management list page, read-only detail view, delete confirmation dialog\n- Interaction patterns: status polling/readiness display, admin vs viewer control visibility, error/validation display\n- Disconnected-environment considerations (no external assets)\n- Design spec ready for frontend implementation; UXD review sign-off\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Wireframes exist for all four surfaces, covering admin and viewer states\n- Wizard wireframes reflect the decided TP field set and backend-combination constraints\n- Designs follow the dashboard's PatternFly 6 design system\n- Design spec is reviewed and signed off by UXD\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- Supporting: P0 create wizard / list / inspect / delete (design input); P1 viewer read-only states; P1 air-gapped (no external assets in designs)\n\nE004:\n\n# Extend Dashboard RBAC and Feature-Flag Manifests for Feature Store Admin CRUD\n\n## Description\nManifest-level changes in odh-dashboard enabling admin CRUD on FeatureStore CRs and progressive rollout of the admin UI: extend the ClusterRole with create/update/patch/delete verbs for feast.dev/featurestores, and add the OdhDashboardConfig feature-flag default gating the Feature Store admin UI.\n\n## Scope\n- Update manifests/core-bases/base/sa-rbac/cluster-role.yaml: add create, update, patch, delete verbs for feast.dev/featurestores (reference featurestore-editor-role for the minimum permission set)\n- Add feature flag default in OdhDashboardConfig for the Feature Store admin UI\n- Verify viewer tier remains read-only (existing featurestore-viewer-role grants get/list/watch only)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- The extended ClusterRole grants create/update/patch/delete on feast.dev/featurestores; applied manifests reconcile cleanly\n- Non-admin users holding only viewer bindings cannot write FeatureStore CRs (verified via K8s RBAC)\n- Clusters without the feature flag enabled show no UI changes (backwards compatibility)\n- No new Go BFF module or external dependency introduced (FIPS posture unchanged)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- P0: create wizard, delete (write verbs enabling CRUD)\n- P1: viewer read-only (K8s-level RBAC enforcement tier)\n\nE005:\n\n# Implement Feature Store Create Form Wizard\n\n## Description\nReact form wizard (PatternFly 6) in odh-dashboard that lets platform admins deploy a new FeatureStore instance by filling a guided form mapped to the FeatureStore CRD (feast.dev/v1) — no YAML or CLI. Submits via the existing /api/k8s pass-through with the user's token. Implements the decided TP field set with schema-driven validation, admin-only access, and full offline/air-gapped operation.\n\n## Scope\n- Guided form wizard: namespace selection, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, scaling parameters (per the decided TP field-set spec)\n- Input validation against CRD OpenAPI schema constraints with inline guidance (required fields, valid backend combinations, scaling prerequisites); server-side rejection errors surfaced in the UI\n- Submission of a valid FeatureStore CR via the /api/k8s pass-through\n- Admin-only access (secureAdminRoute / admin check); create action not available to viewers\n- All form options, validation rules, and assets bundled in static assets (no external network fetches)\n- Feature-flag gating of the wizard surface\n- Validate form fields against the CRD OpenAPI schema at build time (CRD stability mitigation)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- A platform admin can complete the wizard and submit a valid FeatureStore CR from the dashboard with no YAML editing or CLI access\n- Form renders all decided TP fields; invalid combinations are blocked with inline guidance before submission\n- If the K8s API rejects a CR, the validation error is surfaced in the form\n- Non-admin users cannot access the create flow\n- The wizard functions with no external network access (all options/validation bundled)\n- Wizard is hidden unless the feature flag is enabled\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- P0: deploy new FeatureStore instance via guided form wizard\n- P2: inline validation guidance for CRD schema constraints (bundled — same form surface)\n- P1: viewer read-only (admin-only create access)\n- P1: air-gapped operation (bundled form options)\n\nE006:\n\n# Implement Feature Store Management List, Detail, Delete, and Status Views\n\n## Description\nDashboard management surface for existing FeatureStore instances: a list page across accessible namespaces with real-time deployment status, a read-only detail/inspect view, and an admin-initiated delete flow with confirmation. Read/browse available to viewers; write controls admin-only.\n\n## Scope\n- Management list page: name, namespace, deployment status (from .status.conditions), creation timestamp; watch/poll using existing dashboard K8s watch/list patterns for real-time readiness updates without manual refresh\n- Read-only detail view: full FeatureStore CR spec and status (backends, auth mode, scaling, TLS, materialization schedule, conditions); link to Feast UI Route when available\n- Delete flow: confirmation dialog; DELETE via /api/k8s pass-through; operator handles cleanup via finalizers\n- Viewer mode: list/detail visible, create/delete controls hidden based on admin status check\n- Create-action entry point on the list page that opens the creation wizard (coordinate navigation/routing with the wizard work)\n- All UI assets bundled (air-gapped operation); feature-flag gating\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- All FeatureStore instances in accessible namespaces are listed with name, namespace, status, creation timestamp (matching kubectl get featurestores -A for the admin's accessible namespaces)\n- Status column reflects .status.conditions within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle, updating from Deploying to Ready without manual refresh\n- Detail view renders all spec fields and status conditions without truncation\n- Delete with confirmation removes the CR; instance disappears from the list\n- Non-admin users see list/detail without create/delete controls\n- Page functions on a disconnected cluster with no external connectivity\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- P0: view all instances in management page\n- P0: inspect configuration in read-only detail view\n- P0: delete instance with confirmation dialog\n- P0: deployment progress / readiness visible in real time\n- P1: viewer read-only browsing\n- P1: air-gapped operation\n\nE007:\n\n# Validate FeatureStore CRD and Operator Behavior for Dashboard-Created Instances\n\n## Description\nFeature Store Engineering validation of the feast-operator's behavior for instances created/managed via the dashboard (rather than kubect