{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9f1175a7-4565-4f0f-902c-a9415b4552dc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-99469ec322fe3ffd","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-c38t3ptf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E004.md","content":"# Extend Dashboard RBAC and Feature-Flag Manifests for Feature Store Admin CRUD\n\n## Description\n\nManifest-level changes in odh-dashboard that enable admin CRUD operations on `FeatureStore` custom resources and progressive rollout of the Feature Store admin UI: extending the dashboard ClusterRole with write verbs for `feast.dev/featurestores` and adding the `OdhDashboardConfig` feature-flag default that gates the admin UI. No new backend routes or Go modules are introduced — CRUD flows through the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through, which forwards the authenticated user's token so RBAC is enforced at the K8s API level.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Update `manifests/core-bases/base/sa-rbac/cluster-role.yaml` to add `create`, `update`, `patch`, `delete` verbs for `feast.dev/featurestores`, using the feast-operator's `featurestore-editor-role` as the reference for the minimum required permission set\n- Add a feature-flag default in `OdhDashboardConfig` gating the Feature Store admin UI (clusters without the flag see no UI changes)\n- Verify the viewer tier remains read-only — the existing `featurestore-viewer-role` grants only `get`, `list`, `watch` on `featurestores` and `featurestores/status`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The extended ClusterRole grants `create`, `update`, `patch`, `delete` on `feast.dev/featurestores`, and the applied manifests reconcile cleanly\n- A user holding only viewer bindings cannot write `FeatureStore` CRs (verified against the K8s API with the user's token)\n- Clusters with the feature flag disabled show no Feature Store UI changes (backwards compatibility)\n- No new Go BFF module or external dependency is introduced — RBAC changes are manifest-only and the FIPS posture is unchanged\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P0: create wizard and delete HLRs (write verbs enabling admin CRUD)\n- P1: viewer read-only browsing (K8s-level RBAC enforcement tier)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":55901,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac68a93886bffd55","agent_id":"a40e7c224b2cca3e1","session_id":"0ef27685-1ed8-4b23-8ac0-1ea621901635","uuid":"8301f757-ccc2-4937-81c7-a4626a322829","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:46:57.038Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007"}
