{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9f1175a7-4565-4f0f-902c-a9415b4552dc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a83ecb798b884728","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-c38t3ptf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E006.md","content":"# Implement Feature Store Management List, Detail, Delete, and Status Views\n\n## Description\n\nDashboard management surface for existing Feature Store instances: a management page listing all `FeatureStore` CRs across the admin's accessible namespaces with real-time deployment status, a read-only detail/inspect view, and an admin-initiated delete flow with a confirmation dialog. Browsing (list and detail) is available to viewer users; write controls are admin-only. Implemented after the prototype-alignment assessment and the approved UXD designs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Management list page: rows showing name, namespace, deployment status (from `.status.conditions`), and creation timestamp, across all namespaces visible to the user\n- Real-time status updates using the dashboard's existing K8s watch/list patterns, so readiness state reflects deployment progress (\"Deploying\" → \"Ready\") without manual refresh\n- Read-only detail/inspect view: the full `FeatureStore` CR spec (backends, authorization mode, scaling, TLS status, materialization schedule) and current status conditions, with a link to the Feast UI Route when available\n- Delete flow: confirmation dialog, then a `DELETE` request via the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through; the Feast operator handles resource cleanup via finalizers\n- Viewer mode: list and detail views visible to non-admin users with create/delete controls hidden based on the dashboard's admin-status check\n- Create-action entry point on the list page that opens the instance-creation wizard (navigation/routing coordinated with the wizard work)\n- Feature-flag gating; all UI assets bundled for air-gapped operation\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- All `FeatureStore` instances in the user's accessible namespaces are listed with name, namespace, status, and creation timestamp, matching `kubectl get featurestores -A` for those namespaces\n- The status column reflects `.status.conditions` within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle, updating from deploying to ready without manual refresh\n- The detail view renders all spec fields and status conditions without truncation\n- Delete with confirmation removes the `FeatureStore` CR via the K8s API and the instance disappears from the list\n- Non-admin users see the list and detail views without create or delete controls\n- The pages function on a disconnected cluster with no external connectivity\n- Delete operations succeed end-to-end through the pass-through with the extended dashboard ClusterRole (integration with the RBAC manifest change)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P0: view all FeatureStore instances in a dashboard management page\n- P0: inspect the configuration of any instance in a read-only detail view\n- P0: delete a FeatureStore instance with a confirmation dialog\n- P0: deployment progress (readiness status) visible in the dashboard in real time\n- P1: viewer read-only browsing (hidden write controls)\n- P1: air-gapped operation (bundled assets)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":55901,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac68a93886bffd55","agent_id":"a40e7c224b2cca3e1","session_id":"0ef27685-1ed8-4b23-8ac0-1ea621901635","uuid":"5ae57baa-60ba-44ec-a6b7-d3229c374f70","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:47:16.203Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007"}
