{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fdbb4cc32bc5c21","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n3\tepic_count: 8\n4\tcritical_path_length: 4\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8007\n11\t\n12\t**Strategy**: [TP] Feature Store Admin UI — Self-Service Instance Deployment and Management\n13\t\n14\t**Triage**: Not below-threshold (effort M / 3-5 sprints; spans frontend, backend/manifests, design, validation, and documentation work streams across four teams). Not docs-only (primary deliverable is code). Full decomposition performed.\n15\t\n16\t**Staff Engineer Input**: Section present but empty (template placeholder only) — no overrides to apply.\n17\t\n18\t## Epic List\n19\t\n20\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n21\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n22\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E001 | Assess prototype PR #7013 alignment and reuse potential | Investigation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E002 | Decide TP form field scope and supported backend combinations | Investigation | Feature Store Engineering | P0 |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E003 | UXD wireframes and interaction design for Feature Store admin UI | Implementation | UXD Team | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E004 | Extend dashboard RBAC and feature-flag manifests for Feature Store admin CRUD | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E005 | Implement Feature Store create form wizard | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E006 | Implement Feature Store management list, detail, delete, and status views | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E007 | Validate FeatureStore CRD and operator behavior for dashboard-created instances | Implementation | Feature Store Engineering | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E008 | Document the Feature Store admin UI workflow in the RHOAI admin guide | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Documentation Team | P1 |\n30\t\n31\t## Dependency DAG\n32\t\n33\t```mermaid\n34\tgraph TD\n35\t  E001[\"E001 Prototype alignment (Investigation)\"] --> E005\n36\t  E001 --> E006\n37\t  E002[\"E002 Form field scope (Investigation)\"] --> E003\n38\t  E002 --> E005\n39\t  E003[\"E003 UXD design\"] --> E005\n40\t  E003 --> E006\n41\t  E004[\"E004 RBAC + feature-flag manifests\"]\n42\t  E007[\"E007 feast-operator validation\"]\n43\t  E003 --> E008[\"E008 Admin guide docs\"]\n44\t  E004 --> E008\n45\t  E005 --> E008\n46\t  E006 --> E008\n47\t  E007 --> E008\n48\t```\n49\t\n50\tCritical path: E002 → E003 → E005 → E008 (length 4).\n51\t\n52\t## DAG Justification\n53\t\n54\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n55\t| --- | --- | --- |\n56\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate) | Prototype-alignment outcome determines whether the wizard is built by adapting prototype code or from scratch — a `rewrite` gate on implementation approach. |\n57\t| E001 → E006 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate) | Same outcome determines the implementation basis for the management views — `rewrite` gate. |\n58\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 3 / Rule 12 analog | The decided TP field set defines what the create-wizard wireframes must cover; design builds against the decision artifact. |\n59\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate) | The wizard implements the decided field set and backend-combination constraints — `rewrite` gate (bounded outcomes alter wizard scope, not DAG structure, so no branch files; recorded via `gated_by` + `gate_failure_impact`). |\n60\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 12 (artifact → consumer) | Frontend implementation builds against the approved UXD designs. |\n61\t| E003 → E006 | Rule 12 (artifact → consumer) | Frontend implementation builds against the approved UXD designs. |\n62\t| E004 → E005/E006: **no edge** | Rule 15 | Same repo, different areas (kustomize manifests vs React frontend). The RBAC/feature-flag config is not a build-against artifact — integration is enforced by acceptance criteria on the frontend epics (CRUD succeeds with the extended ClusterRole; UI hidden unless flag enabled), never by a DAG edge. |\n63\t| E007 → E005/E006: **no edge** | Step 2 passive-component exception | feast-operator needs no code changes (\"No code changes expected\"); the owning team validates it in parallel. Validation results feed the frontend epics' ACs (operator cleanup, status conditions), not their code. |\n64\t| E003, E004, E005, E006, E007 → E008 | Rule 11 (docs last) | `docs-authoring` epic is blocked by every main-plan Implementation epic; docs describe what was built. |\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n67\t\n68\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n69\t| --- | --- | --- |\n70\t| Deploy new FeatureStore instance via guided form wizard (namespace, registry type, online/offline store, auth mode, scaling) | P0 | E005 (scope decided by E002; schema coverage validated by E007) |\n71\t| View all FeatureStore instances in a management page (name, namespace, status, creation time) | P0 | E006 |\n72\t| Inspect configuration of any instance in read-only detail view | P0 | E006 |\n73\t| Delete a FeatureStore instance with confirmation dialog | P0 | E006 (operator cleanup validated by E007) |\n74\t| Deployment progress / readiness status visible in real time | P0 | E006 (status conditions validated by E007) |\n75\t| Non-admin viewers can browse but not create/delete | P1 | E006 (hidden controls), E005 (admin-only create), E004 (K8s-level RBAC enforcement) |\n76\t| Admin UI functions in disconnected/air-gapped environments | P1 | E005 (bundled form options/validation), E006 (bundled assets), E008 (disconnected deployment instructions) |\n77\t| Inline form validation guidance for CRD schema constraints | P2 | E005 — bundled: same form surface and validation logic as the P0 wizard; splitting would build the same UI surface twice |\n78\t\n79\tAll 8 HLRs are covered; no or