{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83a7ddba031e4429","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n3\ttitle: Decide TP form field scope and supported backend combinations\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: Feature Store Engineering\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Decide TP Form Field Scope and Supported Backend Combinations\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tInvestigation that decides which `FeatureStore` CRD (feast.dev/v1) fields the Technology Preview create wizard exposes — the full CRD spec or a curated subset — and which backend combinations (registry type, online/offline store backends, authorization mode) are supported or restricted for production readiness. The deliverable is a field-set and validation-constraint specification that the create-wizard design and implementation build against. This is a joint product and engineering decision owned by the PM and Feature Store Engineering.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Enumerate the `FeatureStore` CRD spec fields from the CRD OpenAPI schema: registry type, online store backend (Redis, PostgreSQL, DynamoDB, SQLite), offline store backend, authorization mode, TLS settings, scaling configuration, materialization scheduling\n34\t- Decide the TP-exposed field set (full spec vs curated subset), with rationale for excluded fields\n35\t- Identify backend combinations that should be restricted or flagged in the form (e.g., SQLite as development-only and not suitable for production)\n36\t- Deliver a field-set and validation-constraint specification for the create wizard\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A field-set specification exists listing every `FeatureStore` CRD field exposed in the TP wizard, with rationale for any excluded fields\n41\t- Restricted or unsupported backend combinations are enumerated with user-facing guidance\n42\t- The decision is confirmed by the PM and Feature Store Engineering\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- P0: guided form wizard field coverage (this decision defines the wizard's scope)\n47\t- P2: inline validation guidance for CRD schema constraints (this decision defines the constraint source)\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9be413476f1a86f","agent_id":"a885c71eb67262f30","session_id":"0ef27685-1ed8-4b23-8ac0-1ea621901635","uuid":"0add0546-5dad-455b-a5d9-a1007909ce4f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:50:52.940Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-83a7ddba031e4429","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
