{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91384144b5706cba","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E006\n3\ttitle: Implement Feature Store management list, detail, delete, and status views\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the prototype is not architecturally aligned, the management\n16\t    views are built from scratch following established dashboard patterns instead\n17\t    of adapting prototype code; the delivered pages and acceptance criteria are unchanged\n18\t    either way.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 8\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Implement Feature Store Management List, Detail, Delete, and Status Views\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tDashboard management surface for existing Feature Store instances: a management page listing all `FeatureStore` CRs across the admin's accessible namespaces with real-time deployment status, a read-only detail/inspect view, and an admin-initiated delete flow with a confirmation dialog. Browsing (list and detail) is available to viewer users; write controls are admin-only. Implemented after the prototype-alignment assessment and the approved UXD designs.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Management list page: rows showing name, namespace, deployment status (from `.status.conditions`), and creation timestamp, across all namespaces visible to the user\n45\t- Real-time status updates using the dashboard's existing K8s watch/list patterns, so readiness state reflects deployment progress (\"Deploying\" → \"Ready\") without manual refresh\n46\t- Read-only detail/inspect view: the full `FeatureStore` CR spec (backends, authorization mode, scaling, TLS status, materialization schedule) and current status conditions, with a link to the Feast UI Route when available\n47\t- Delete flow: confirmation dialog, then a `DELETE` request via the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through; the Feast operator handles resource cleanup via finalizers\n48\t- Viewer mode: list and detail views visible to non-admin users with create/delete controls hidden based on the dashboard's admin-status check\n49\t- Create-action entry point on the list page that opens the instance-creation wizard (navigation/routing coordinated with the wizard work)\n50\t- Feature-flag gating; all UI assets bundled for air-gapped operation\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- All `FeatureStore` instances in the user's accessible namespaces are listed with name, namespace, status, and creation timestamp, matching `kubectl get featurestores -A` for those namespaces\n55\t- The status column reflects `.status.conditions` within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle, updating from deploying to ready without manual refresh\n56\t- The detail view renders all spec fields and status conditions without truncation\n57\t- Delete with confirmation removes the `FeatureStore` CR via the K8s API and the instance disappears from the list\n58\t- Non-admin users see the list and detail views without create or delete controls\n59\t- The pages function on a disconnected cluster with no external connectivity\n60\t- Delete operations succeed end-to-end through the pass-through with the extended dashboard ClusterRole (integration with the RBAC manifest change)\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- P0: view all FeatureStore instances in a dashboard management page\n65\t- P0: inspect the configuration of any instance in a read-only detail view\n66\t- P0: delete a FeatureStore instance with a confirmation dialog\n67\t- P0: deployment progress (readiness status) visible in the dashboard in real time\n68\t- P1: viewer read-only browsing (hidden write controls)\n69\t- P1: air-gapped operation (bundled assets)\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9be413476f1a86f","agent_id":"a885c71eb67262f30","session_id":"0ef27685-1ed8-4b23-8ac0-1ea621901635","uuid":"199b60d5-f398-4143-a1e1-eb2ec92a3815","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:51:01.765Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-91384144b5706cba","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3cda6beed097fba","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E005\n3\ttitle: Implement Feature Store create form wizard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the TP field-scope decision or prototype-alignment outcome\n17\t    diverges from the assumed basis, the wizard's field set and implementation basis\n18\t    are rewritten to match the decided spec; if no curated subset is agreed, the wizard\n19\t    falls back to exposing the full CRD field set with schema-driven validation.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: 1\n26\t  external_dependency: 0\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 7\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Implement Feature Store Create Form Wizard\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tReact form wizard (PatternFly 6) in odh-dashboard that lets a platform administrator deploy a new `FeatureStore` instance by filling out a guided form mapped to the `FeatureStore` CRD (feast.dev/v1) — no YAML editing or CLI access required. The wizard implements the decided TP field set with schema-driven validation, submits through the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through using the user's own token, is restricted to admin users, and operates fully in disconnected/air-gapped environments. Implemented after the prototype-alignment assessment, the form field-scope decision, and the approved UXD designs.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Guided form wizard covering the decided TP field set: namespace selection, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling parameters\n46\t- Client-side input validation derived from the CRD OpenAPI schema, with inline guidance for required fields, valid backend combinations, and scaling prerequisites; form fields validated against the CRD OpenAPI schema at build time (CRD version-bump mitigation)\n47\t- Submission of a valid `FeatureStore` CR via the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through; if the K8s API rejects the CR, the server-side validation error is surfaced in the form\n48\t- Admin-only access to the create flow (dashboard admin-status check / `secureAdminRoute` pattern); create action not available to viewer users\n49\t- All form options, validation rules, and UI assets bundled in the dashboard's static assets — no external network fetches (air-gapped support)\n50\t- Feature-flag gating of the wizard surface\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A platform admin can complete the wizard and submit a valid `FeatureStore` CR from the dashboard with no YAML editing or CLI access, with the form rendering all decided TP fields without error\n55\t- Invalid input (required fields, unsupported backend combinations, scaling prerequisites) is blocked before submission with inline guidance\n56\t- A K8s API rejection of a submitted CR is surfaced as an actionable error in the form\n57\t- Non-admin users cannot access the create flow\n58\t- The wizard functions on a disconnected cluster with no external network access — no form options, validation rules, or UI assets require external connectivity\n59\t- The wizard surface is hidden unless the feature flag is enabled\n60\t- Create/delete operations succeed end-to-end through the pass-through with the extended dashboard ClusterRole (integration with the RBAC manifest change)\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- P0: deploy a new FeatureStore instance from the dashboard via a guided form wizard\n65\t- P2: inline form validation guidance for CRD schema constraints (bundled — same form surface and validation logic as the P0 wizard)\n66\t- P1: viewer read-only (admin-only create access)\n67\t- P1: air-gapped operation (bundled form options and validation)\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9be413476f1a86f","agent_id":"a885c71eb67262f30","session_id":"0ef27685-1ed8-4b23-8ac0-1ea621901635","uuid":"84ecafde-8ec2-47df-a8e3-b82d1fa34b42","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:51:01.767Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3cda6beed097fba","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
