{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-85362018cec79e98","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E005\n3\ttitle: Implement Feature Store create form wizard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the TP field-scope decision or prototype-alignment outcome\n17\t    diverges from the assumed basis, the wizard's field set and implementation basis\n18\t    are rewritten to match the decided spec; if no curated subset is agreed, the wizard\n19\t    falls back to exposing the full CRD field set with schema-driven validation.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: 1\n26\t  external_dependency: 0\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 7\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Implement Feature Store Create Form Wizard\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tReact form wizard (PatternFly 6) in odh-dashboard that lets a platform administrator deploy a new `FeatureStore` instance by filling out a guided form mapped to the `FeatureStore` CRD (feast.dev/v1) — no YAML editing or CLI access required. The wizard implements the decided TP field set with schema-driven validation, submits through the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through using the user's own token, is restricted to admin users, and operates fully in disconnected/air-gapped environments. Implemented after the prototype-alignment assessment, the form field-scope decision, and the approved UXD designs.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Guided form wizard covering the decided TP field set: namespace selection, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling parameters\n46\t- Client-side input validation derived from the CRD OpenAPI schema, with inline guidance for required fields, valid backend combinations, and scaling prerequisites; form fields validated against the CRD OpenAPI schema at build time (CRD version-bump mitigation)\n47\t- Submission of a valid `FeatureStore` CR via the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through; if the K8s API rejects the CR, the server-side validation error is surfaced in the form\n48\t- Admin-only access to the create flow (dashboard admin-status check / `secureAdminRoute` pattern); create action not available to viewer users\n49\t- All form options, validation rules, and UI assets bundled in the dashboard's static assets — no external network fetches (air-gapped support)\n50\t- Feature-flag gating of the wizard surface\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A platform admin can complete the wizard and submit a valid `FeatureStore` CR from the dashboard with no YAML editing or CLI access, with the form rendering all decided TP fields without error\n55\t- Invalid input (required fields, unsupported backend combinations, scaling prerequisites) is blocked before submission with inline guidance\n56\t- A K8s API rejection of a submitted CR is surfaced as an actionable error in the form\n57\t- Non-admin users cannot access the create flow\n58\t- The wizard functions on a disconnected cluster with no external network access — no form options, validation rules, or UI assets require external connectivity\n59\t- The wizard surface is hidden unless the feature flag is enabled\n60\t- Create/delete operations succeed end-to-end through the pass-through with the extended dashboard ClusterRole (integration with the RBAC manifest change)\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- P0: deploy a new FeatureStore instance from the dashboard via a guided form wizard\n65\t- P2: inline form validation guidance for CRD schema constraints (bundled — same form surface and validation logic as the P0 wizard)\n66\t- P1: viewer read-only (admin-only create access)\n67\t- P1: air-gapped operation (bundled form options and validation)\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a73d21eb81e9941c","agent_id":"a222a03520a2c6bb0","session_id":"0ef27685-1ed8-4b23-8ac0-1ea621901635","uuid":"ac93d8ac-1833-4957-8be7-a7b7cdf926a3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:57:25.469Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-85362018cec79e98","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
