{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac629d56b9ef90a8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Assess prototype PR #7013 alignment and reuse potential'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Assess Prototype PR #7013 Alignment and Reuse Potential\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tInvestigation that resolves whether the existing engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) implements the approach described in the strategy, and how much of it can be reused in the formal implementation. The outcome determines the implementation basis for the Feature Store admin UI pages — adapting prototype code versus building from scratch following established dashboard patterns — and is a prerequisite for starting the frontend implementation work.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Review the prototype pull request against the strategy's technical approach: K8s API pass-through CRUD via `/api/k8s/*`, the existing `/api/featurestores` read proxy, the RBAC model, feature-flag gating, and page structure (management list, create wizard, detail view, delete flow)\n34\t- Identify which prototype components are directly reusable, which diverge from the formal approach, and which capabilities are absent\n35\t- Produce a written alignment mapping and a reuse/migration recommendation for the formal implementation\n36\t- Confirm the assessment and recommendation with the Dashboard and Feature Store engineering leads\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A written assessment exists that maps each prototype capability to the strategy's approach, classified as aligned, divergent, or absent\n41\t- A reuse recommendation with rationale is delivered, stating explicitly whether the formal implementation should adapt the prototype or start from established dashboard patterns\n42\t- Any architectural divergence that would change the formal implementation approach is called out explicitly\n43\t- The assessment is confirmed by the Dashboard and Feature Store engineering leads\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- Supporting: all P0 HLRs (create wizard, management list, inspect view, delete, deployment progress) — this investigation determines how, not whether, they are built\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90eae1365c80b058","agent_id":"ab79cda22a64c12c2","session_id":"0ef27685-1ed8-4b23-8ac0-1ea621901635","uuid":"6c2ee9a9-a950-44c1-840e-d83ddcda6728","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:00:39.484Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac629d56b9ef90a8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8007"}
