{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6f5a7ea56bd788f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E004\n3\ttitle: Extend dashboard RBAC and feature-flag manifests for Feature Store admin CRUD\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 8\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Extend Dashboard RBAC and Feature-Flag Manifests for Feature Store Admin CRUD\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tManifest-level changes in odh-dashboard that enable admin CRUD operations on `FeatureStore` custom resources and progressive rollout of the Feature Store admin UI: extending the dashboard ClusterRole with write verbs for `feast.dev/featurestores` and adding the `OdhDashboardConfig` feature-flag default that gates the admin UI. No new backend routes or Go modules are introduced — CRUD flows through the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through, which forwards the authenticated user's token so RBAC is enforced at the K8s API level.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Update `manifests/core-bases/base/sa-rbac/cluster-role.yaml` to add `create`, `update`, `patch`, `delete` verbs for `feast.dev/featurestores`, using the feast-operator's `featurestore-editor-role` as the reference for the minimum required permission set\n38\t- Add a feature-flag default in `OdhDashboardConfig` gating the Feature Store admin UI (clusters without the flag see no UI changes)\n39\t- Verify the viewer tier remains read-only — the existing `featurestore-viewer-role` grants only `get`, `list`, `watch` on `featurestores` and `featurestores/status`\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- The extended ClusterRole grants `create`, `update`, `patch`, `delete` on `feast.dev/featurestores`, and the applied manifests reconcile cleanly\n44\t- A user holding only viewer bindings cannot write `FeatureStore` CRs (verified against the K8s API with the user's token)\n45\t- Clusters with the feature flag disabled show no Feature Store UI changes (backwards compatibility)\n46\t- No new Go BFF module or external dependency is introduced — RBAC changes are manifest-only and the FIPS posture is unchanged\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- P0: create wizard and delete HLRs (write verbs enabling admin CRUD)\n51\t- P1: viewer read-only browsing (K8s-level RBAC enforcement tier)\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90eae1365c80b058","agent_id":"ab79cda22a64c12c2","session_id":"0ef27685-1ed8-4b23-8ac0-1ea621901635","uuid":"e95543dd-de0d-4962-a845-904944cc64de","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:00:44.835Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6f5a7ea56bd788f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8007"}
