{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9866952cf9f94d67","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E006\n3\ttitle: Implement Feature Store management list, detail, delete, and status views\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the prototype is not architecturally aligned, the management\n16\t    views are built from scratch following established dashboard patterns instead\n17\t    of adapting prototype code; the delivered pages and acceptance criteria are unchanged\n18\t    either way.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 8\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Implement Feature Store Management List, Detail, Delete, and Status Views\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tDashboard management surface for existing Feature Store instances: a management page listing all `FeatureStore` CRs across the admin's accessible namespaces with real-time deployment status, a read-only detail/inspect view, and an admin-initiated delete flow with a confirmation dialog. Browsing (list and detail) is available to viewer users; write controls are admin-only. Implemented after the prototype-alignment assessment and the approved UXD designs.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Management list page: rows showing name, namespace, deployment status (from `.status.conditions`), and creation timestamp, across all namespaces visible to the user\n45\t- Real-time status updates using the dashboard's existing K8s watch/list patterns, so readiness state reflects deployment progress (\"Deploying\" → \"Ready\") without manual refresh\n46\t- Read-only detail/inspect view: the full `FeatureStore` CR spec (backends, authorization mode, scaling, TLS status, materialization schedule) and current status conditions, with a link to the Feast UI Route when available\n47\t- Delete flow: confirmation dialog, then a `DELETE` request via the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through; the Feast operator handles resource cleanup via finalizers\n48\t- Viewer mode: list and detail views visible to non-admin users with create/delete controls hidden based on the dashboard's admin-status check\n49\t- Create-action entry point on the list page that opens the instance-creation wizard (navigation/routing coordinated with the wizard work)\n50\t- Feature-flag gating; all UI assets bundled for air-gapped operation\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- All `FeatureStore` instances in the user's accessible namespaces are listed with name, namespace, status, and creation timestamp, matching `kubectl get featurestores -A` for those namespaces\n55\t- The status column reflects `.status.conditions` within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle, updating from deploying to ready without manual refresh\n56\t- The detail view renders all spec fields and status conditions without truncation\n57\t- Delete with confirmation removes the `FeatureStore` CR via the K8s API and the instance disappears from the list\n58\t- Non-admin users see the list and detail views without create or delete controls\n59\t- The list page's Create action navigates to the instance-creation wizard route when the feature flag is enabled and the user is a platform admin, and is hidden for non-admin users or when the flag is disabled\n60\t- The pages function on a disconnected cluster with no external connectivity\n61\t- Delete operations succeed end-to-end through the pass-through with the extended dashboard ClusterRole (integration with the RBAC manifest change)\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- P0: view all FeatureStore instances in a dashboard management page\n66\t- P0: inspect the configuration of any instance in a read-only detail view\n67\t- P0: delete a FeatureStore instance with a confirmation dialog\n68\t- P0: deployment progress (readiness status) visible in the dashboard in real time\n69\t- P1: viewer read-only browsing (hidden write controls)\n70\t- P1: air-gapped operation (bundled assets)\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90eae1365c80b058","agent_id":"ab79cda22a64c12c2","session_id":"0ef27685-1ed8-4b23-8ac0-1ea621901635","uuid":"14634b7a-a6ac-4a86-bde8-3da0a3f90ccb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:00:49.671Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9866952cf9f94d67","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8007"}
