{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b570046e9d14b81b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E007\n3\ttitle: Validate FeatureStore CRD and operator behavior for dashboard-created instances\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: Feature Store Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Validate FeatureStore CRD and Operator Behavior for Dashboard-Created Instances\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tFeature Store Engineering validation of the feast-operator's behavior for `FeatureStore` instances created and managed through the dashboard (rather than kubectl or GitOps): CRD webhook validation sufficiency for UI-submitted resources, reconciliation correctness, finalizer-based cleanup on delete, and status-condition surfacing. The feast-operator itself requires no code changes unless validation finds gaps — this epic delivers the validation evidence and any remediation recommendations.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Validate that `FeatureStore` CRD webhook validation is sufficient for UI-submitted resources — invalid CRs are rejected with actionable messages the dashboard can surface\n38\t- Confirm the operator reconciles dashboard-created CRs identically to kubectl-created ones (the operator watches the CRD, not the creation method)\n39\t- Confirm delete-time cleanup of all operator-owned resources (Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, CronJobs, HPAs, PDBs, RBAC resources, Routes) via finalizers\n40\t- Confirm `.status.conditions` surface deployment readiness in a form the dashboard can display\n41\t- Deliver a validation report with remediation recommendations to the dashboard team if any gap is found\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- A validation report exists covering webhook validation, reconciliation of dashboard-created CRs, delete-time cleanup, and status-condition surfacing\n46\t- Each validation check has an explicit pass/fail result with evidence\n47\t- Any identified gap is documented with a recommended remediation in the feast-operator\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- Supporting: P0 create wizard (CRD schema and webhook validation coverage for form-submitted resources)\n52\t- Supporting: P0 delete (operator cleanup of owned resources)\n53\t- Supporting: P0 deployment progress (status conditions available for dashboard display)\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90eae1365c80b058","agent_id":"ab79cda22a64c12c2","session_id":"0ef27685-1ed8-4b23-8ac0-1ea621901635","uuid":"9d32b4db-d71c-4134-9fab-afe15bfdf547","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:00:53.825Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b570046e9d14b81b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8007"}
